# The story scenes and the result screens, ported from data/dialogue.json (prompt 03).
# Directions before a line: [scene office|void|glade|keep] [sleep 0-3] [book] [slime] [knight]
# [sfx name]. A line inside <<if next == "tutorial">> is said only when the scene leads there.
# Each line's i18n key is story.intro.<node>.<n>. See docs/WRITING.md.

== intro ==
[scene office] [sleep 0] : 11:58 pm. The quarterly report is still running.
[scene office] [sleep 1] Ada: Nobody reads these dashboards anyway. SQL is just... busywork.
[scene office] [sleep 2] Ada: I'll just close my eyes... until it reaches 100%...
[scene office] [sleep 3] [sfx flatline] : The progress bar stops at 99%. So does {player.name}'s heart.
[scene void] : ...
[scene glade] Ada: Grass? Why is the sky a table? Why does it have so many columns?
[scene glade] [book] [sfx book] Grimoire: Welcome to the Kingdom of Codd, witch. Here the world is a database, and magic is querying.
[scene glade] [book] Ada: A... talking book?
[scene glade] [book] Grimoire: Your Grimoire. Here, magic is not waved: it is written. Every spell is a query.
[scene glade] [book] Ada: I write SQL all day. How hard can it be?
<<if next == "tutorial">>
[scene glade] [book] Grimoire: Then show me. Before you meet anything with teeth, practice on something made of straw.
<<endif>>
<<if next == "slime">>
[scene glade] [book] Grimoire: My right page holds only four rows. You pay for every spell you summon, but only the rows you can read take effect.
<<endif>>
<<if next == "slime">>
[scene glade] [book] Grimoire: Never written a query? In battle, press F3 or click GUIDE: I will show you what to write, and how to read my pages.
<<endif>>
<<if next == "slime">>
[scene glade] [book] Grimoire: And you will learn the rest from the first thing that wants to eat you.
<<endif>>
<<if next == "slime">>
[scene glade] [book] [slime] : Something round and green wobbles out of the bushes: the ASTERISK SLIME!
<<endif>>

== knight_intro ==
[scene glade] [book] Grimoire: LIMIT is yours, witch. The next guardian is not beaten with fewer spells, but with the right ones.
[scene keep] [book] : The Filter Keep. Its gate opens only for what is relevant.
[scene keep] [book] [knight] [sfx ward_up] Sir Wherewell: Halt! I am Sir Wherewell, Knight of the Filter. My Ward of Relevance stops every spell that does not matter.
[scene keep] [book] [knight] Sir Wherewell: Only a spell of the element I am weak to can get through. Do you know which one, witch?
[scene keep] [book] [knight] Ada: I know dozens of spells now. How do I cast only the right ones?
[scene keep] [book] [knight] Grimoire: Look at him first with SELECT * FROM enemies and find his weakness. Then watch his book: he never casts without WHERE.

== victory ==
: The Asterisk Slime melts into a puddle of rows.
Ada: One word. LIMIT. And the page behaves.

== confused ==
: The fight dissolves into confusion: there is nothing left to win.
Grimoire: A backup would have brought it back. Next time, rewind (F6).

== defeat ==
: {player.name}'s HP hits zero. The Slime wobbles triumphantly.
Grimoire: Even the best witches overflow sometimes. Again?

== knight_victory ==
: Sir Wherewell kneels and opens the gate.
Ada: WHERE. Ask only for what you need.

== knight_defeat ==
: {player.name}'s HP hits zero. The Knight lowers his blade.
Grimoire: Spells that are not super-effective bounce off. Filter for his weakness.

== battle_tip ==
: New to SQL? Press F3 for the spell guide.

== end_of_slice ==
: End of the vertical slice. Thank you for playing!
